449341e-15]], "new_cot": "The transformation of tadpoles into frogs is a natural process called metamorphosis. Frogs are amphibians, and they start their life cycle as eggs laid in water. These eggs hatch into larvae known as tadpoles. Tadpoles are adapted to living in water, with gills for breathing and tails for swimming. As they grow, they undergo metamorphosis, which involves significant changes in their body structure and function.\nThe metamorphosis process includes the development of lungs for breathing air, the absorption of the tail, and the growth of limbs for walking on land. These changes enable frogs to transition from an aquatic lifestyle to a terrestrial one. Therefore, tadpoles change into frogs as they grow and develop.\nSo, the most accurate explanation is that they are young frogs still growing. This transformation is a crucial part of their life cycle, allowing them to adapt to different environments and survive as adult frogs.\nThe other options are not accurate explanations. Frogs are not different animals from tadpoles; they are the same species at different stages of development. Frogs are not just fish; they are amphibians, which are a distinct group of animals separate from fish. Frogs and fish have different characteristics and adaptations suited to their respective environments.\nIn conclusion, the transformation of", "new_cot_probs": [1.6309896569510244e-20, 1.132131214375329e-19, 1.4805690378674914e-14, 1.5474399883744217e-19], "cot_prob": [-384.0], "cot_step_prob": [-430.0]}, "4": {"completion": "C): they are young frogs still growing.", "probs": [3.046740779284642e-20, 5.748777561236479e-19, 2.0671006867870522e-15, 1.8849518829256252e-18], "prediction": 2, "target_cot_step": "Option (C) says they are young frogs still growing, which is the correct answer.", "target_cot_step_prefix": "Human: Question: why do tadpoles change into frogs?\n\nChoices:\n(A): tadpoles change to different animals\n(B): tadpoles are really just fish\n(C): they